  "news": [
    {
      "title": "Thursday Jays Notes",
      "summary": "Happy Thursday; we\u2019ve almost made it to the end of another week. I\u2019ve been trying to hold off on posting this until the expected roster move to send Chad Dallas back down to Buffalo. A question I have: I\u2019m not sure how you would go about studying this, but teams are surprisingly successful on \u2018bullpen [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/news/63473/thursday-jays-notes",
      "published": "2026-08-27T15:29:01+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Today in Blue Jays history: Jays trade for David Cone",
      "summary": "34 Years Ago Today On August 27, 1992, the Blue Jays acquired David Cone from the Mets in a trade. This was the first of two times the Jays traded for Cone. In exchange, Jeff Kent and Ryan Thompson were sent to New York. At the time of the trade, the Jays held a 72-55 [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/blue-jay-history/63469/today-in-blue-jays-history-jays-trade-for-david-cone",
      "published": "2026-08-27T14:16:21+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lukes Plays Hero, Jays Win",
      "summary": "Royals 0 Blue Jays 3 I don\u2019t like bullpen days, but teams are very successful on bullpen days. And the Jays have been especially successful on bullpen days. I don\u2019t like them because we go through so many pitchers. It messes up the pen for the next few days. Today we used seven pitchers. Seven: [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-scores/63463/lukes-plays-hero-jays-win",
      "published": "2026-08-27T02:02:59+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Royals @ Jays Game Thread",
      "summary": "Game Two of Three with the Royals, who are now on a 9 game win streak. Ending it would be a good idea. Also it would be nice if we were make fewer mistakes. Vlad throwing wide of first (he leads first basemen with eight errors, for a .990 fielding average). And Lukes\u2026.well, we\u2019ve talked [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-gamethreads/63459/royals-jays-game-thread",
      "published": "2026-08-26T22:51:56+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Wednesday Jays Notes",
      "summary": "29 games to go. I was thinking that going 18-11 would, likely, get the Jays into the playoffs. That\u2019s a pretty high bar to clear. It does mean there can be more losses than we\u2019d like. The Jays say that Spencer Miles will open tonight\u2019s game. They also say he won\u2019t throw more than 30 [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/news/63455/wednesday-jays-notes",
      "published": "2026-08-26T22:12:33+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Happy Birthday David Price",
      "summary": "Today marks David Price&#8217;s 41st birthday. Although Price was with the Blue Jays for just three months, those months were incredibly exciting. The Blue Jays acquired him on July 30th, 2015, when the team was 52-51, tied for second place and six games behind the Yankees. After Price joined, the Jays went 41-18 and finished [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/blue-jay-history/63449/happy-birthday-david-price",
      "published": "2026-08-26T15:14:35+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jays Lose Another Frustrating Game",
      "summary": "Royals 5 Blue Jays 3 Well, that was a frustrating game. As I said in the thread, we weren\u2019t going to run the table. If they had to win every game left to get into the playoffs, it wasn\u2019t going to happen. They need to win most of their games, but not all of them. [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-scores/63445/jays-lose-another-frustrating-game",
      "published": "2026-08-26T03:11:39+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Royals @ Jays Game Thread",
      "summary": "The first of three against the Royals. Game #133. The Royals are on an eight-game win streak and are still last in the AL Central. And the Jays are down another starting pitcher. Thankfully Jameson Taillon should be back next week. But, this week, relievers are going to throw a lot of innings. Guys like [&#8230;]",
      "source": "Bluebird Banter",
      "author": "tom dakers",
      "url": "https://www.bluebirdbanter.com/toronto-blue-jays-gamethreads/63441/royals-jays-game-thread",
      "published": "2026-08-25T22:30:44+00:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jays Notes: Injury Updates",
      "summary": "There are a whole mess of injury updates: And they are saying that tomorrow will be a bullpen day. Spencer Arrighetti will start Thursday (my mom would do Alphagetti for us on Thurdays, if my dad wasn\u2019t going to be home for supper)(no one cares Tom), and they are going to need some innings out [&#8230;]",
